+      "origin": "New teaching material prepared under the owner's 15 October 2026 authorisation to use internet equivalents; not recovered school-source text. It supersedes, in delivery, the original First-Term row 'Sexually Transmitted Diseases (STDs)', which tells a person with HIV not to become pregnant, lists circumcision among skin-cutting risks without distinguishing clean medical circumcision, omits antiretroviral treatment and condoms, and says AIDS 'cannot be cured' without explaining that treatment allows a long healthy life. The original row is preserved unchanged in the audit record. It is school teaching, not personal medical advice.",
